      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Pandas issues a warning instead of silently failing because failing silently could lead to subtle, hard-to-diagnose bugs where an unintended write operation modifies your original data without notice. This \"helpful\" behavior stems from a design choice in early pandas versions (pre-0.25) where views were mutable, allowing users to accidentally pass data references without getting feedback.\n\nWhile it can feel like over-caution, the deeper issue is about avoiding \"accidental mutability\" in column operations, which ensures that your filtered data remains isolated from the source object and prevents potential data corruption or unexpected behavior when shared across different parts of your code. The warning forces you to explicitly acknowledge this distinction, promoting more predictable and robust data manipulation.",
